      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Choosing a tag from the list writes it whole: <act + Tab gives <action \"\"/>, the caret between the quotes",
      "excerpt": "Choosing a tag from the list writes it whole: <act + Tab gives <action \"\"/>, the caret between the quotes",
      "text": "good.  Let's add a space between the end quote and the |>",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-14T09:51:48.051Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-14T10:08:17.660Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  a tag with a quoted name, chosen from the suggestions, is now written <code>&lt;action \"|\" /&gt;</code>, with a space after the end quote (Spanish <code>&lt;acción \"|\" /&gt;</code>), and the hover help shows it that way too.</p>\n<p>Tags with no name stay <code>&lt;divider/&gt;</code>, as most of the examples write them.  Say if you want those spaced too.</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-14T21:36:49.202Z",
          "text": "yes, always a space before the />\n\nAndm,",
          "edited": "2026-11-14T21:37:10.595Z"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-14T22:08:07.230Z",
          "html": "<p>Will do:  every tag that closes itself is written with a space before its <code>/&gt;</code>, as in <code>&lt;divider /&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;icon | /&gt;</code>.</p><p>That covers the suggestions list, the new space-after-a-tag help (T68), the palette and paste.  The editor-autotag agent is on it now.</p>"
        }
      ],
